note `edit` was written before it. A is a name (a global is error 19, a fresh array 27); o, then k, are
note ulong values. Checks, in this order: o <= len A (CMP Xo, Xlen; B.HI trap 3), then k <= len A - o (SUB,
note CMP, B.HI trap 3); the wrapped o + k is never formed. The part is a view of A + o * size with count k:
note an edit when A is writable (local or edit) and no `view` was written, else a view. It goes only to an
note unsized parameter (error 7). Out as arrarg; rt is A, so for error 19 the part counts as its base.
fn arrpart f ulong pi ulong md ulong to void
