note `holds NAME dup32` at top level before the first fn (names pass). NAME is type 64 + index: a value of
note it comes only from `seal NAME v` inside the function NAMEmk returning NAME (else error 28), `open v`
note gives the T value, and the listed operations (rotr/rotl with a T count, and/or/xor of two NAME
note values) keep NAME; anything else on it, a T value or a number where NAME is needed, an array of it and
note the entry function's parameters and result are error 7. With holds, seal checks high32 == low32
