note ir_forg: the for loop over counter ctr = 0 below kr. N = 0: the plain loop, head: lt ctr kr -> body | exit.
note Else the guarded loop, the C oracle's shape (omegese.c guarded_loop): a ulong counter cnt = 0 as well; head:
note lt ctr kr -> guard | exit; guard: ge cnt N -> trap 4 | body; body starts with cnt = add cnt 1. Literals and
note blocks are made in the oracle's order (literals are shared). The latch adds 1 to ctr (ir_end kind 3). The
note for frame (kind 3: head h, exit ex, counter ctr): the counter, bound last, leaves scope at the end.
note The literals 0 and 1 are made first (shared; ir_lit returns the same register again), then the counters.
note om4 holds 16 registers per function, so the guard blocks reuse names already dead: ty is the guard block
note and w the trap block (both after ir_bind); cnt is 0 only in the plain loop (two literals precede it).
