note ======== Native x86-64 semantic backend ========
note Intel SDM volume 2 instruction entries MOV, LEA, CALL, RET, Jcc, SETcc, MOVSX,
note MOVZX, ADD, SUB, IMUL, DIV, IDIV, SHL, SHR, SAR, SYSCALL; volume 2 chapter 2
note supplies REX, ModRM and SIB. No A64 word decoding occurs in this backend.
fn xb a ulong b ulong c ulong to void
emitb uchar a
emitb uchar b
emitb uchar c
end

fn xword v ulong to void
emitb uchar and v 255
emitb uchar and shr v 8 255
emitb uchar and shr v 16 255
emitb uchar and shr v 24 255
end

fn ximm r ulong v ulong to void
emitb uchar add 72 shr r 3
emitb uchar add 184 and r 7
xword v
xword shr v 32
end

note Hardware registers are private emitter operands. Language values are RBP slots.
fn xrr op ulong d ulong s ulong to void
emitb uchar add add 72 shl shr s 3 2 shr d 3
emitb uchar op
emitb uchar add add 192 shl and s 7 3 and d 7
end

fn xmem op ulong r ulong b ulong off ulong to void
emitb uchar add add 72 shl shr r 3 2 shr b 3
emitb uchar op
emitb uchar add add 128 shl and r 7 3 and b 7
if eq and b 7 4
emitb 36
end
xword off
end

